&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE 4. PENSION PLANS AND OTHE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;R POSTRETIREMENT BENEFIT PLANS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 120%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company contributed $3 million in cash to the pension plan during the three months ended March&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;31, 2026. The Company expects to contribute $10 million in total in 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 120%; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company uses a December 31 measurement date for its defined benefit pension and other postretirement benefit plans. The following table sets forth the components of net periodic benefit costs for the three months ended March 31 (dollars in millions):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
